<h1>Joe Holberg</h1>
<p>Fintech founder and former West Side teacher. Candidate for mayor of Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p>Founded the wealth advisory firm Spring, sold to Mariner in 2023, after teaching middle school math on the West Side; 38, a first-generation college graduate who lives in Lincoln Park with his wife and two children. The first candidate to enter, in October 2025, and filed 32,000 signatures.</p>
<p><a href="/directdemocracy/app/candidate/1oCf1IYduwev0n0JU8tgdNzcZyx2">Full platform, open to comments</a></p>
<p><a href="https://www.joeforchicago.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website (joeforchicago.com)</a></p>
<h2>What sets them apart</h2>
<p>Only Holberg: A plan to reverse Chicago&#39;s population loss: more visitors and big events, short work stints in the city, and one sign-up for new residents.</p>
<p>Property taxes: Freeze them, then lower them. Kitover and Kelly say much the same; Giannoulias would hold the levy flat; Nee will not rule out an increase.</p>
<p>Schools: Names one target, the 30 percent chronic absentee rate.</p>
<p>With most of the field: On housing, policing, transit, and pensions the platform lists goals most candidates share.</p>
<h2>Where they split from the field</h2>
<p>Property taxes: Freeze or lower them, with Kelly and Kitover. Hold the city&#39;s levy flat: Giannoulias. An increase is not off the table: Nee.</p>
<h2>In their words</h2>
<ul>
<li>Reverse Chicago&#39;s population loss with more visitors, big events, and an easier move for new residents. <q>I am running for Mayor of Chicago because I have a vision to turn our economic engine back on</q> (<a href="https://www.nbcchicago.com/news/local/who-is-running-for-chicago-mayor-what-to-know-as-nominating-period-ends/4008071/" rel="nofollow noopener">NBC Chicago, Oct. 2026</a>)</li>
<li>Freeze property taxes, then lower them. <q>If we grow and expand our tax base, not only will we have more revenue, but each of us will pay less,</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/chicago-mayoral-candidate-joe-holberg/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Aug. 5, 2026</a>)</li>
<li>Bring down the 30 percent chronic absentee rate in the public schools. <q>I was a teacher on the West Side, first and foremost,</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/chicago-mayoral-candidate-joe-holberg/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Aug. 5, 2026</a>)</li>
<li>Fix the CTA as a daily rider, starting with clean trains. <q>When riders sit in cars that reek of urine, their first thought is whether they can take an Uber next time.</q> (<a href="https://chi.streetsblog.org/2026/07/16/op-ed-from-mayoral-candidate-joe-holberg-chicago-deserves-a-safe-clean-cta-here-are-five-commonsense-solutions-from-a-daily-rider" rel="nofollow noopener">Streetsblog Chicago op-ed, July 16, 2026</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Campaign money</h2>
<ul>
<li>Committee: Joe For Chicago</li>
<li>Raised: $155K</li>
<li>Spent: $201K</li>
<li>Cash on hand: $1.1M</li>
<li>Raised July 1 to Sept. 30, 2026; spent Jan. 1 to Sept. 30, 2026. The committee owes the candidate $950,000 in loans, about 70 percent of what it has raised. <a href="https://elections.il.gov/CampaignDisclosure/CommitteeDetail.aspx?id=40876" rel="nofollow noopener">Source</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Money figures are each committee&#39;s quarterly reports to the Illinois State Board of Elections: spent is total expenditures from January 1 to September 30, 2026 (or since the committee formed), cash is funds available on September 30.</p>
<h2>Support</h2>
<p>1.7% of likely voters in the ChicagoSpeaks poll, Sept. 2026 (Mansueto Institute / NORC). 8.5 points of support per $1 million spent.</p>
<h2>On money</h2>
<p>Would balance the budget first, grow the tax base so each person pays less, freeze and then lower property taxes, and start cutting with the city&#39;s vehicle purchases.</p>
<ul>
<li><q>If we grow and expand our tax base, not only will we have more revenue, but each of us will pay less,</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/chicago-mayoral-candidate-joe-holberg/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Aug. 5, 2026</a>)</li>
<li><q>We buy $25 million too many vehicles a year,</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/chicago-mayoral-candidate-joe-holberg/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Aug. 5, 2026</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Pizza</h2>
<p>No position on record.</p>
<h2>Also on the record</h2>
<ul>
<li>Was homeless in college and slept in his car; his parents were a lighting technician and a school aide. (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/chicago-mayoral-candidate-joe-holberg/" rel="nofollow noopener">cbsnews.com</a>)</li>
</ul>
